-- One of two UNRELATED modules each declaring a record TYPE spelled `Cfg`, with
-- the SAME two `Int` field names at OPPOSITE indices.  Same-typed on purpose: the
-- disjoint-field and divergent-type shapes make a wrong pick LOUD, which is what
-- blinded the original unit-3 corpus.  Here a wrong pick is a WRONG NUMBER.
public export data Cfg = { a : Int, b : Int }

-- Exported as a VALUE, not a type: `entry` never writes `Cfg`.
export mkA : Cfg
mkA = Cfg { a = 11, b = 22 }
